    "question": {
      ":question/id": "644b5634-4b66-5b37-aa13-102c5b8f9bd9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $9\\times 12$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=8$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=12.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 8+\\text{nullity}(A) & =12 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =12-8 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
